{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system","id":1391070,"title":"Question about 3 edition combat system.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-23T16:41:53-07:00","id":1391070,"title":"Question about 3 edition combat system.","content":"While I have read most of the 3 ed core, I have never actually played exalted third.<br /> <br /> After reading the systems, it looked like the combat system was awesome for epic 1v1 duels but it will hold poorly in a 3v1 scenario, for example, since initiative crash/drain will make the outnumbered side near harmless, or at least, WAY less capable of inflicting damage.<br /> <br /> Can somebody who has actually played 1 edition, second edition and third edition confirm or deny this for me?<br /> <br /> Also to explain/clarify things if my assumption was very far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T16:58:27-07:00","id":1391071,"title":"","content":"3e can do outnumbered fights just fine, but like any edition of Exalted, what's fighting matters.<br /> <br /> Numbers help, but a bunch of farmers that have never fought before aren't going to be taking down a Dawn any time soon. Even with just mortals, a highly skilled fighter with good equipment is probably going to take out three thugs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:04:14-07:00","id":1391072,"title":"","content":"Third Edition makes it harder for the 1 to go &quot;these odds are unfavourable... I should fight with my eyes closed&quot;. You can still do it and win near instantly though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:13:19-07:00","id":1391074,"title":"","content":"It worked out pretty well in my experience. Granted, the only time any of my players ended up in a fight with more than 2 on 1 odds it had been trivial enemies, so can't say how far it goes before numbers destroy the players on that front. (I think a few rounds in enemies started just getting obliterated by the anima flux.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:13:28-07:00","id":1391075,"title":"","content":"A Dawn caste can easily win a fight against 5 opponents in the first round of combat before they even act, so yes, absolutely you can win on those odds.<br /> <br /> Even without being a Dawn though, if their damage doesn't exceed your soak they're going to have a really damn hard time keeping your initiative low, while at the same time if your damage far exceeds their soak you're going to be crashing and killing them very easily. That's also assuming everyone can easily land hits, which is a bad assumption.<br /> <br /> If you're evenly matched and outnumbered 3 to 1...well the game models pretty well how it would go being outnumbered by people just as strong as you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:14:27-07:00","id":1391076,"title":"","content":"Hm. It seems I was wrong.<br /> <br /> At first glance it looked like the outnumbered guy would be drained from all initiative constantly unless massive essence sink in defending itself.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:19:50-07:00","id":1391077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391076#post1391076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first glance it looked like the outnumbered guy would be drained from all initiative constantly unless massive essence sink in defending itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms like Fivefold Bulwark Stance, Hail Shattering Practice and Against The World Stance make defending yourself against even fairly powerful opponents almost free. With Fivefold Bulwark Stance you not only ignore almost all penalties to your defense, but it makes Dipping Swallow cost only 1m to activate, and ignore literally all penalties to defense, AND raise your parry by 1. So if you're eating 3 attacks a turn, you spend 3m per turn to raise your parry to 8, no matter what. Then past that there's charms like Hail Shattering Practice, that let you retroactively raise your parry if you get hit, and Against the World Stance, which gives you motes back every time an enemy misses you.<br /> <br /> So with all that it's mega easy to go even 5v1 against most enemies.<br /> <br /> You may run into a bit of a hitch if 5 Essence 5 Immaculate Grandmasters all gang up on you at once or something though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:35:53-07:00","id":1391079,"title":"","content":"Its also pretty easy to get an absurd Join Battle roll, ensuring you start first, which can then turn into splatting a couple dudes right from the get-go. Its easy enough to build for this exact tactic in Melee","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:03:11-07:00","id":1391085,"title":"","content":"If you're not even trying to optimize, and just take Melee charms that look cool, you'll eventually get pretty good at nova-ing a couple weaker foes to start and then slowly grinding down the rest with the Fivefold Bulwark Stance strategy DrLoveMonkey mentioned. (This may even be the intended way to play...) Other charm trees probably aren't quite as good at this, but defeating multiple weaker foes is still not a rare occurrence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T00:45:34-07:00","id":1391141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system#post1391070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the systems, it looked like the combat system was awesome for epic 1v1 duels but it will hold poorly in a 3v1 scenario, for example, since initiative crash/drain will make the outnumbered side near harmless, or at least, WAY less capable of inflicting damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda?<br /> <br /> In Exalted, you play one of the most powerful beings in existence.<br /> <br /> 90% of foes don't beat you by being more powerful than you, they beat you by ganging up on you.<br /> <br /> And absent Charms, this is a tactic that works. (Resetting Initiative, Initative Shift, Onslaught, etc.)<br /> <br /> This means a pack of Claw Striders can bring down a Tyrant Lizard. Not &quot;unscathed&quot;, but they can do it.<br /> <br /> The idea of ganging up on one's betters runs perversely through Exalted -- the Exalted ganged up on the Primordials, the Dragon-Blooded ganged up on the Solars, the Raksha ganged up on the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> But, there are mitigation factors. If you are familiar with 1E/2E, you are familiar with the concept of Extras. 3E folds Extras into battlegroups (then folds battlegroups into the regular combat system and runs them like a single character). So your hero vs twelve bandits isn't a 12-on-one fight: it's one hero vs one battlegroup. 3E also has trivial opponents, who don't do anything but look awesome when you explode them.<br /> <br /> With Charms, as others have discussed, you can mitigate many of the disadvantages to being outnumbered. This is just like in 1E where Solars had scene-long defensive charms.<br /> <br /> That said, the power tiers of 2E no longer exist. Powerscales have been compressed back to something like 1E, maybe a little flatter: Yes you have Charms, your enemies have Charms too. <br /> <br /> If not mechanically optimizing, a Dragon-Blooded is a credible threat to a Solar, one-on-one. If you are outnumbered 3-on-1, you might want to consider retreat.<br /> <br /> (This isn't true if you optimize: an optimized Solar is going to walk over Dragon-Blooded six-on-one.)<br /> <br /> If you want to get a handle on how combat works, check out the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena\">Exalted Arena thread</a> (fair warning, some of my early fights have rules errors in around mote regeneration).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-24-2020, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:53:59-07:00","id":1391165,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I will buy the book and give it a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T08:39:55-07:00","id":1391197,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, with a party of PCs I find that 3 NPCs vs a PC basically never happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-24-2020, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:26:25-07:00","id":1391335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391197#post1391197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, with a party of PCs I find that 3 NPCs vs a PC basically never happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have 2 PCs and went 2 PCs vs. 6ish NPCs, which is similar, but I can't imagine, with a full circle, going up against 15 NPCs very often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:57:42-07:00","id":1391343,"title":"","content":"I was assuming the OP was asking more in the other direction of the PCs outnumbering their enemies as something the system can handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:43:06-07:00","id":1391379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391343#post1391343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming the OP was asking more in the other direction of the PCs outnumbering their enemies as something the system can handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are Solars invested into combat, especially if they are combat-optimized, then it is very hard to create an enemy that will give them a challenge 3 on 1. There are few such enemies in the books, narratively speaking there are not supposed to be many creatures this powerful in the world, and it is not easy to design your own (at least not one that creates a fight that is both challenging and fun).<br /> <br /> If the PCs are DBs, there do exist enemies which give them a challenge 3 on 1 - I would think for any given DB builds there should always be a Solar build that can give them a challenge without killing them.<br /> <br /> But people who have posted heavily in the Arena thread probably know more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:55:57-07:00","id":1391382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391379#post1391379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are Solars invested into combat, especially if they are combat-optimized, then it is very hard to create an enemy that will give them a challenge 3 on 1. There are few such enemies in the books, narratively speaking there are not supposed to be many creatures this powerful in the world, and it is not easy to design your own (at least not one that creates a fight that is both challenging and fun).<br /> <br /> If the PCs are DBs, there do exist enemies which give them a challenge 3 on 1 - I would think for any given DB builds there should always be a Solar build that can give them a challenge without killing them.<br /> <br /> But people who have posted heavily in the Arena thread probably know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is kind of a sliding scale.<br /> <br /> There was a combat run in the Exalted:Arena thread of Ess 2 Solar Invincible Sword Princess with <b>all </b>the Melee charms (so pretty much the strongest Ess 2 supernal combatant you could make) vs 3 immaculates at Ess 3, the 3 Immaculates won (one died due to 1st round alpha strike).<br /> <br /> I like to use this as a convenient benchmark as here we can see that even if you build an absolute cleaver of a character (the strongest Ess 2 Melee combatant in the game, arguably), 3 v 1 is still going to beat you until higher essence, it would seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:08:54-07:00","id":1391389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391343#post1391343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming the OP was asking more in the other direction of the PCs outnumbering their enemies as something the system can handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that being the case, that will depend enormously on the PCs involved. If you have a group of 5 PC Solars, and they all took physical primary, dex 5, ability 5 with a specialty, artifact weapons and armor, and 5-6 combat charms, you're going to get a group that can kill basically anything if they're fresh and full of motes, health levels, and willpower.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you've got 3 Dragonblooded PCs, only one of whom has a combat ability with more than 3 dots, and the other two have like 1-2 combat charms each, there are a lot of published enemies in the antagonist section of the book that will be able to fight that whole circle and win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:57:09-07:00","id":1391404,"title":"","content":"I've run combats with PCs against a Single Baddie and it's, pardon my Old Realm here, <i>fucking terrible</i>. I've got a Single Point/War/Sail Eclipse with a steel-willed battlegroup, a Twilight Melee Sorcerer with a Full Survival Tree Familiar, and a Presence Supernal Zenith. It is a goddamn nightmare to run anything short of Octavian at them. I had to install a custom charm/rule that the Sole Baddie only loses 1 initiative when withered (Solars <i>gain </i>full initiative, the baddie just only drops 1) and negate Onslaught penalties or there is no way to dig yourself out of the hole of having all your initiative constantly stolen from you. Even high soak doesn't help that much, because you are constantly bleeding from a being attacked 4 times a turn, and your motes are basically at a 4-to-1 disadvantage. <br /> <br /> The <i>other</i> problem that comes up in actual play is you invariably have a spectrum of &quot;The Jesus of Murder&quot; to &quot;Super Tax Accountant&quot; heroes, and if you <i>do</i> throw Octavian, Ahlat, Fakharu, or whoever at them then you the ST have to walk a fine line of &quot;Instantly Splat the Socialite&quot; or &quot;Use Razor Nightmare Hurricane on the Dawn, use Gentle Pillow Toss on the Twilight&quot;. It can also break immersion if not done carefully. <br /> <br /> A PC Solar 1 v 3ing some Dynasts is going to nova one down instantly almost every time because its the best tactic, a 3 Dynast PCs against an NPC Solar are probably not going to have one player draw the short straw and get decapitated before they can even move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:19:40-07:00","id":1391418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391077#post1391077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charms like Fivefold Bulwark Stance, Hail Shattering Practice and Against The World Stance make defending yourself against even fairly powerful opponents almost free. With Fivefold Bulwark Stance you not only ignore almost all penalties to your defense, but it makes Dipping Swallow cost only 1m to activate, and ignore literally all penalties to defense, AND raise your parry by 1. So if you're eating 3 attacks a turn, you spend 3m per turn to raise your parry to 8, no matter what. Then past that there's charms like Hail Shattering Practice, that let you retroactively raise your parry if you get hit, and Against the World Stance, which gives you motes back every time an enemy misses you.<br /> <br /> So with all that it's mega easy to go even 5v1 against most enemies.<br /> <br /> You may run into a bit of a hitch if 5 Essence 5 Immaculate Grandmasters all gang up on you at once or something though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say it's &quot;easy&quot;. It's a very specific build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:19:40-07:00","id":1391419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391077#post1391077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charms like Fivefold Bulwark Stance, Hail Shattering Practice and Against The World Stance make defending yourself against even fairly powerful opponents almost free. With Fivefold Bulwark Stance you not only ignore almost all penalties to your defense, but it makes Dipping Swallow cost only 1m to activate, and ignore literally all penalties to defense, AND raise your parry by 1. So if you're eating 3 attacks a turn, you spend 3m per turn to raise your parry to 8, no matter what. Then past that there's charms like Hail Shattering Practice, that let you retroactively raise your parry if you get hit, and Against the World Stance, which gives you motes back every time an enemy misses you.<br /> <br /> So with all that it's mega easy to go even 5v1 against most enemies.<br /> <br /> You may run into a bit of a hitch if 5 Essence 5 Immaculate Grandmasters all gang up on you at once or something though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say it's &quot;easy&quot;. It's a very specific build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T23:02:36-07:00","id":1391428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391404#post1391404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>other</i> problem that comes up in actual play is you invariably have a spectrum of &quot;The Jesus of Murder&quot; to &quot;Super Tax Accountant&quot; heroes, and if you <i>do</i> throw Octavian, Ahlat, Fakharu, or whoever at them then you the ST have to walk a fine line of &quot;Instantly Splat the Socialite&quot; or &quot;Use Razor Nightmare Hurricane on the Dawn, use Gentle Pillow Toss on the Twilight&quot;. It can also break immersion if not done carefully.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this mostly a shortcoming of the antagonists we have because there's a few tricks available among the various charmsets.<br /> <br /> Also some of the NPCs are on the verge of being effective antagonists but lack critical components to get there with no direction to help an inexperienced Storyteller make the most of it (this critique can be made of any edition of Exalted). The Nephwrack for example is blighted by the lack of a good dice adder to keep it alive long enough before Dawn of Dead Stars starts to seriously worry people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:03:00-07:00","id":1391434,"title":"","content":"There's that mile high volcano monster that can be ganged up on. <br /> <br /> Otherwise... not really. You are playing some of the most powerful beings in existence. If you outnumber your enemy as well then that's just kinda cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:09:16-07:00","id":1391436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391428#post1391428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider this mostly a shortcoming of the antagonists we have because there's a few tricks available among the various charmsets.<br /> <br /> Also some of the NPCs are on the verge of being effective antagonists but lack critical components to get there with no direction to help an inexperienced Storyteller make the most of it (this critique can be made of any edition of Exalted). The Nephwrack for example is blighted by the lack of a good dice adder to keep it alive long enough before Dawn of Dead Stars starts to seriously worry people.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for a decent fight I'd run two Nephwracks, a Deathknight, a zombie battlegroup and a battlegroup of hungry ghosts. Zombies out front.<br /> <br /> One Nephwrack starts immaterial, and they drop Clinging Shadow Miasma and the other drops Dawn of Dead Stars on turn one. The Abyssal Commands the zombies to Engage the PCs.<br /> <br /> Turn 2, the immaterial Nephwrack orders the hungry ghosts in, and the Abyssal attacks the most appropriate PC. If the zombies are still alive, the material Nephwrack can command them too (if the PCs brought a battlegroup then maybe they can cast Death of Obsidian Butterflies instead). <br /> <br /> No reason for the other Nephwrack to materialize. They can distort spells, drop Corrupted Words or what-have-you. Generally, both Nephwracks can just keep their distance -- make the PCs battle through difficult terrain and Engaging battlegroups in the dark as the Nephwracks Reflexive move to keep at range. Strike and fade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-25-2020, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:44:21-07:00","id":1391510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391382#post1391382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it is kind of a sliding scale.<br /> <br /> There was a combat run in the Exalted:Arena thread of Ess 2 Solar Invincible Sword Princess with <b>all </b>the Melee charms (so pretty much the strongest Ess 2 supernal combatant you could make) vs 3 immaculates at Ess 3, the 3 Immaculates won (one died due to 1st round alpha strike).<br /> <br /> I like to use this as a convenient benchmark as here we can see that even if you build an absolute cleaver of a character (the strongest Ess 2 Melee combatant in the game, arguably), 3 v 1 is still going to beat you until higher essence, it would seem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you disagree with in what I said - I think you might still be thinking about 1 enemy vs 3 PCs?<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that for a group of 3 Dragonblooded PCs, e.g. those 3 immaculates, one could make a Solar NPC that could challenge them without killing them - in this case, Invincible Sword Princess with a little bit less alpha strike ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391404#post1391404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>other</i> problem that comes up in actual play is you invariably have a spectrum of &quot;The Jesus of Murder&quot; to &quot;Super Tax Accountant&quot; heroes, and if you <i>do</i> throw Octavian, Ahlat, Fakharu, or whoever at them then you the ST have to walk a fine line of &quot;Instantly Splat the Socialite&quot; or &quot;Use Razor Nightmare Hurricane on the Dawn, use Gentle Pillow Toss on the Twilight&quot;. It can also break immersion if not done carefully..</div> </div> </div> </div>I increasingly feel like character creation for Solar Exalted games should not usually involve choosing to play a combat expert or a socialite or whatever, but look more like choosing together what activities the whole party will usually engage in (like &quot;combat, social enocunters, stealth&quot;) and making sure all characters are competent in all those things. One reason is that it's hard to make an encounter where characters of different power levels have fun. Another is that a lot of Exalted's systems seem to be more fun when the characters involved are less powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:50:31-07:00","id":1391512,"title":"","content":"Yes, I was talking about the PC outnumbering the baddie in a 3 to 1.<br /> <br /> Yes. what sorcerous overlord said is exactly what I feared.<br /> <br /> 3What johndoe said its a good way to make &quot;1&quot; abyssal challenge 3 PC, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T12:26:46-07:00","id":1391526,"title":"","content":"The biggest limitation compared to previous editions is that The Mask of Winters isn't in the corebook antagonists section, every other returning NPC there is beefed up significantly compared to 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> The lone Abyssal fighting an entire circle of Solars has never worked for me (especially a 2nd edition Abyssal who was basically Solar that had been spayed) 2.0 perfect spam made such a character less a &quot;spooky scary boss&quot; and more a cockroach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-25-2020, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T12:37:56-07:00","id":1391529,"title":"","content":"3e is better than 2e in that regard at least, barring Deathlords and maybe one or two other things in 2e that haven\u2019t been printed yet in 3e. The super untouchable elder ghosts who know every single Solar charm with Essence 10 have, likely, been toned down a bit, but the fey and demons and stuff have been tuned up. Partly due to the fact that only dawns can get better than Essence 1 combat charms at chargen, so you don\u2019t have everyone in the party with Invincible Fury of the Dawn and a grand goremaul.<br /> On the other hand the problem still exists that your character can spend 90% of their chargen resources on being a sorcerer, and if they spend the last 10% on being a warrior they\u2019re basically good enough to kill almost anything in a 1v1 fight.<br /> <br /> Edit: actually lioness might be right, there\u2019s no published enemies that powerful except Mahicara maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-25-2020, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:31:03-07:00","id":1391551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391512#post1391512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I was talking about the PC outnumbering the baddie in a 3 to 1.<br /> <br /> Yes. what sorcerous overlord said is exactly what I feared.<br /> <br /> 3What johndoe said its a good way to make &quot;1&quot; abyssal challenge 3 PC, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take what Sorcerous Overlord said with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> That's not really a core problem with 3e as a system, but with Solars having access to as much power as they do; and has always been an issue with Exalted.<br /> <br /> Hell, it's a problem that goes well past Exalted to most point-buy systems where PCs can vary wildly in their proficiency in any given situation. <br /> <br /> 3e's general combat mechanics give plenty of tools for a group of PCs fighting a single enemy to be fun and exciting as there's enough defense in the game to avoid numbers being an automatic win.<br /> <br /> But as I said off the bat, what's fighting matters. Getting ganged up on by a bunch of Solars is bad news for almost anyone in the setting by design. There are very few things in Creation that are supposed to be able to stand up to five Solars at once.<br /> <br /> I also think the &quot;Octavian splats everyone else,&quot; problem is a bit overstated. 3e Solars have a surprisingly broad number of ways to be relevant in combat without being the PCs' combat heavy. A lot of non-combat abilities still have some combat utility Charms, there's a lot of good low investment combat ability Charms, and ways to help take down the epic big bads meant to challenge a group of Solars. Sure you can't force the players to take anything, but the investment to not being a liability in a fight against such enemies is small enough that they should at least have enough defenses to ensure something that can be a challenge for a combat maxed out Dawn isn't going to insta-kill everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T16:07:30-07:00","id":1391564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391436#post1391436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for a decent fight I'd run two Nephwracks, a Deathknight, a zombie battlegroup and a battlegroup of hungry ghosts. Zombies out front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're a support monster, the heavy artifact armour and the daiklave create a misleading impression of physical might for inexperienced Storytellers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T17:42:58-07:00","id":1391571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391551#post1391551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, it's a problem that goes well past Exalted to most point-buy systems where PCs can vary wildly in their proficiency in any given situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah that's the kernel of my problem balancing 4 Solars on 1 Enemy. Well, that's one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3e's general combat mechanics give plenty of tools for a group of PCs fighting a single enemy to be fun and exciting as there's enough defense in the game to avoid numbers being an automatic win. </div> </div> </div>So there's a bit to unpack here:<br /> E3E has many defenive tools: True.<br /> It's easy enough to get those tools: True.<br /> Those charms keep high numbers from being an automatic win: Debatable<br /> PCs will reliably take those options: <b>Your Mileage May Vary. </b><br /> <br /> My current cirlce has a Twilight Bureaucracy Supernal who barely invested in Thrown and only has 1 Dodge Charm* because Exalted lets him just play a super bureaucrat and he thought that was neat. The Zenith has 0 combat or defense charms because she's like a Midsommar version of Moses- Presence, Socialize, Integrity. She has a DeeB bodyguard specifically so that she wont have to personally fight but its not in character for a Super Cult Prophet to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391510#post1391510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I increasingly feel like character creation for Solar Exalted games should not usually involve choosing to play a combat expert or a socialite or whatever, but look more like choosing together what activities the whole party will usually engage in (like &quot;combat, social enocunters, stealth&quot;) and making sure all characters are competent in all those things. One reason is that it's hard to make an encounter where characters of different power levels have fun. Another is that a lot of Exalted's systems seem to be more fun when the characters involved are less powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not disagreed more strongly to any single post on this forum. Exalted isn't about the charms, or the cool battle mechanic, or lore, or the laser kung fu, <i>Exalted is about playing a Legendary Hero</i>. It's Gilgamesh, Moses, Archimedes, Marco Polo, and Hattori Hanzo walking the earth and getting into Larger than Life adventures, where each of their individual super-abilities can help save the day in unique ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-25-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T18:18:42-07:00","id":1391577,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Sorcerous Overlord;n1391571]Those charms keep high numbers from being an automatic win: Debatable<br /> PCs will reliably take those options: <b>Your Mileage May Vary. </b><br /> <br /> The ability to keep high numbers from being an automatic win isn't really debatable as much as up to the ST (without as much advice as the game should be giving them on such matters). Picking and/or designing an NPC that can fend off a group of starting Solars is doable, even if it takes some system mastery to accomplish (but that's true of previous editions as well).<br /> <br /> PCs not taking defensive stuff doesn't really impact how hard it is for the PCs to gang up on a single target. Even for some of the nastier antagonists out there, ignoring the Melee Dawn Blender in your face to try to pick on the completely non-combat character isn't exactly a smart idea.<br /> <br /> And while you can't force players to take anything... a game that outright says you should take at least 2-5 combat Charms at start due to the default level of violence means if you have players that aren't even doing that then you should be having a serious Session 0 chat about the expectations for your game, and how dedicated to non-combat characters are going to function in high stakes action scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have not disagreed more strongly to any single post on this forum. Exalted isn't about the charms, or the cool battle mechanic, or lore, or the laser kung fu, <i>Exalted is about playing a Legendary Hero</i>. It's Gilgamesh, Moses, Archimedes, Marco Polo, and Hattori Hanzo walking the earth and getting into Larger than Life adventures, where each of their individual super-abilities can help save the day in unique ways. </div> </div> </div>This seems a bit hard to square.<br /> <br /> Charms, cool battle mechanics, and so on are how everyone's individual super-abilities let them save the day in unique ways over their larger than life adventures. What the game is about, and how the game goes about manifesting that, are tightly connected things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:30:19-07:00","id":1391592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391571#post1391571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not disagreed more strongly to any single post on this forum. Exalted isn't about the charms, or the cool battle mechanic, or lore, or the laser kung fu, <i>Exalted is about playing a Legendary Hero</i>. It's Gilgamesh, Moses, Archimedes, Marco Polo, and Hattori Hanzo walking the earth and getting into Larger than Life adventures, where each of their individual super-abilities can help save the day in unique ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely possible that this is a dumb idea - I really haven't thought of it that much (and playing my character as a legendary hero instead of a really really fancy dude is not something I'm so good at yet).<br /> <br /> But let me try to explain myself.<br /> <br /> While some of those characters are highly specialized, others have a reasonable spread of different abilities. Hattori Hanzo the actual real life figure had impressive displays of Melee, War, some social skills, and Stealth. <br /> <br /> You can be a legendary hero in Exalted taking 3-5 Charms in a particular Ability. You can be a legendary hero at multiple things.<br /> <br /> If you take 15 combat Charms, you might well feel less like a legendary hero than taking 5 combat Charms, because your challenging combats will be slower, more grueling, and less frequent.<br /> <br /> Your character will also have a bit more room to grow in play this way.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a character who is super specialized in a particular thing, sure, play a character who is super specialized in a particular thing. But if you're not sure what the concept for your character should be like, it might be a better idea to think of a character concept who can do a bunch of different things.<br /> <br /> A separate point: If some of your players don't want to take combat charms because they have noncombat-themed characters, then they probably don't want to participate in combat, and won't mind sitting out for a bit during combat encounters, so combat balance isn't as much of an issue, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T23:48:08-07:00","id":1391639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391436#post1391436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for a decent fight I'd run two Nephwracks, a Deathknight, a zombie battlegroup and a battlegroup of hungry ghosts. Zombies out front.<br /> <br /> One Nephwrack starts immaterial, and they drop Clinging Shadow Miasma and the other drops Dawn of Dead Stars on turn one. The Abyssal Commands the zombies to Engage the PCs.<br /> <br /> Turn 2, the immaterial Nephwrack orders the hungry ghosts in, and the Abyssal attacks the most appropriate PC. If the zombies are still alive, the material Nephwrack can command them too (if the PCs brought a battlegroup then maybe they can cast Death of Obsidian Butterflies instead). <br /> <br /> No reason for the other Nephwrack to materialize. They can distort spells, drop Corrupted Words or what-have-you. Generally, both Nephwracks can just keep their distance -- make the PCs battle through difficult terrain and Engaging battlegroups in the dark as the Nephwracks Reflexive move to keep at range. Strike and fade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with you except I dont think I would run 2 different battlegroup of samey monsters (low power undead enemies). I know they dont have the same lvl of power, but I think they are close enough compared to the rest to prefer having a unique battlegroup with a bit more Size","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:24:10-07:00","id":1391657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391510#post1391510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I increasingly feel like character creation for Solar Exalted games should not usually involve choosing to play a combat expert or a socialite or whatever, but look more like choosing together what activities the whole party will usually engage in (like &amp;quot;combat, social enocunters, stealth&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and making sure all characters are competent in all those things. One reason is that it's hard to make an encounter where characters of different power levels have fun. Another is that a lot of Exalted's systems seem to be more fun when the characters involved are less powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391571#post1391571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not disagreed more strongly to any single post on this forum. Exalted isn't about the charms, or the cool battle mechanic, or lore, or the laser kung fu, <i>Exalted is about playing a Legendary Hero</i>. It's Gilgamesh, Moses, Archimedes, Marco Polo, and Hattori Hanzo walking the earth and getting into Larger than Life adventures, where each of their individual super-abilities can help save the day in unique ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either of these can work and be a lot of fun: both appoaches have their own challenges.<br /> <br /> Either way, however, you all need to be on the same page on what everyone's expectations of the game are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391639#post1391639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree with you except I dont think I would run 2 different battlegroup of samey monsters (low power undead enemies). I know they dont have the same lvl of power, but I think they are close enough compared to the rest to prefer having a unique battlegroup with a bit more Size</div> </div> </div> </div>The only RAW issue, which if you are happy to handwave then I'd encourage you to, is that Materialized beings can't see or hear Immaterial beings. So your Immaterial Nephwrack can't give orders to one large battlegroup.<br /> <br /> But I certainly wouldn't oppose rolling the undead into a single battlegroup once they have Materialized. I love the idea of running as few battlegroups as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:34:43-07:00","id":1391659,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Yeah this is a point indeed, but for the sake of handling less stuff I think I would ignore that should the scenario ever arise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:27:56-07:00","id":1391728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391404#post1391404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've run combats with PCs against a Single Baddie and it's, pardon my Old Realm here, <i>fucking terrible</i>. I've got a Single Point/War/Sail Eclipse with a steel-willed battlegroup, a Twilight Melee Sorcerer with a Full Survival Tree Familiar, and a Presence Supernal Zenith. It is a goddamn nightmare to run anything short of Octavian at them. I had to install a custom charm/rule that the Sole Baddie only loses 1 initiative when withered (Solars <i>gain </i>full initiative, the baddie just only drops 1) and negate Onslaught penalties or there is no way to dig yourself out of the hole of having all your initiative constantly stolen from you. Even high soak doesn't help that much, because you are constantly bleeding from a being attacked 4 times a turn, and your motes are basically at a 4-to-1 disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391197#post1391197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, with a party of PCs I find that 3 NPCs vs a PC basically never happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>These two posts pretty much sum up my experience running Ex3. I had multiple encounters in a row where I never so much as connected with a single withering attack, much less had my players feeling like they were actually challenged. &quot;Three gods of war vs four Solars&quot; or &quot;one primordial storm behemoth three Solars&quot; should have been good encounters, but the former got smeared across the map in, like, two turns, and the latter (Mata-Yadh with a few tweaks) only lasted as long as it did because the players had to destroy its legs one by one.<br /> <br /> It's true that Solars, even fresh out of character creation, are meant to be on the high end of the setting's power scale... but it shouldn't be true that five brand-new Solars can curbstomp beings as potent as the god of war for <i>a quarter of the world</i>. That they <i>can </i>easily take Ahlat as presented is an artifact of a combat system that-- from the ground up-- makes being outnumbered hugely disadvantageous. It's not about onslaught penalties, it's not even about action economy-- it's the link between health and offensive ability.<br /> <br /> And if you try to avoid that and have reasonably powerful foes that actually outnumber the party... running a dozen goblins in 5e D&amp;D can be a pain; running a dozen fair folk cataphracts or something is so much worse. When your combat system already trends slow (both from complexity, and from the amount of back-and-forth involved in resolving a single charm-boosted attack), doubling or tripling the number of actors is just... painful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I really enjoy Ex3, even the combat... but I never want to run or play the game with more than two PCs again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:18:02-07:00","id":1392003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1391728#post1391728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's true that Solars, even fresh out of character creation, are meant to be on the high end of the setting's power scale... but it shouldn't be true that five brand-new Solars can curbstomp beings as potent as the god of war for <i>a quarter of the world</i>. That they <i>can </i>easily take Ahlat as presented is an artifact of a combat system that-- from the ground up-- makes being outnumbered hugely disadvantageous. It's not about onslaught penalties, it's not even about action economy-- it's the link between health and offensive ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... the Exalted corebook walks you through, step by step, how to make a &quot;properly terrifying Exalted assassin&quot;. Melee 4, no artifact weapon, Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike as his only charms from Combat Abilities. Pages 129-131.<br /> <br /> I absolutely guarantee that your PCs overspeced for combat.<br /> <br /> Because if you are running a Dawn (with say 7 combat Charms), this &quot;properly terrifying&quot; Night, a Brawl 3 Zenith, an Archery 2 Eclipse, and a Dodge 3 Twilight then Ahlat, a couple of Brides and a couple of god-blooded aurochs (use mundane elephant stats) would absolutely work.<br /> <br /> That said, I take your point about linking health to offense. (I would encourage NPCs to alpha strike.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-28-2020, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T13:34:40-07:00","id":1392035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392003#post1392003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... the Exalted corebook walks you through, step by step, how to make a &quot;properly terrifying Exalted assassin&quot;. Melee 4, no artifact weapon, Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike as his only combat charms. Pages 129-131.<br /> <br /> I absolutely guarantee that your PCs overspeced for combat.<br /> <br /> Because if you are running a Dawn (with say 7 combat Charms), this &quot;properly terrifying&quot; Night, a Brawl 3 Zenith, an Archery 2 Eclipse, and a Dodge 3 Twilight then Ahlat, a couple of Brides and a couple of god-blooded aurochs (use mundane elephant stats) would absolutely work.<br /> <br /> That said, I take your point about linking health to offense. (I would encourage NPCs to alpha strike.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That tells me how to make an Exalted <i>PC. </i>The QC section of the antagonists book gives you benchmarks for numbers, but doesn't have any help for Charms beyond &quot;eh, copy a few existing ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for my PCs... iirc, they generally had 3-5 dots in Dexterity, 5 dots in their chosen combat skill, and 4-6 combat Charms-- all dead easy to do at character creation, while leaving more than enough room for their primary specialties. I suggested those as a guideline, to make sure that no-one wound up underpowered and sidelined during combat scenes that could take two hours of table time to play out. If &quot;a third of your starting resources to combat&quot; is beyond the limit of what the system expects to handle, I'd argue that's an issue with the system, not my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 05-27-2020, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:00:37-07:00","id":1392043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392003#post1392003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent Strike and Fire and Stones Strike as his only combat charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not counting Reed in the Wind, Drifting Leaf Elusion, Reflex Sidestep Technique, Ox-Body Technique, Blinding Battle Feint, and Stalking Wolf Attitude as combat charms?<br /> <br /> Sensory Acuity Prana is a combat charm for some characters but not for this one because he is presumably using Blinding Battle Feint to Join Battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T22:10:41-07:00","id":1392118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392035#post1392035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my PCs... iirc, they generally had 3-5 dots in Dexterity, 5 dots in their chosen combat skill, and 4-6 combat Charms-- all dead easy to do at character creation, while leaving more than enough room for their primary specialties. I suggested those as a guideline, to make sure that no-one wound up underpowered and sidelined during combat scenes that could take two hours of table time to play out. If &quot;a third of your starting resources to combat&quot; is beyond the limit of what the system expects to handle, I'd argue that's an issue with the system, not my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that it's a problem, but it is also possible to make characters like this<br /> <br /> Dawn who's an old guard captain, and before that a soldier. Trained in the use of the sword to an insane degree, and a bow as well. Of course in cases where he has none of those, or where they're taken from him, he's got to be good with his mitts too.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Dawn<br /> <br /> Phys +8bp<br /> 5/5/3<br /> <br /> Soci<br /> 3/4/2<br /> <br /> Ment +3bp<br /> 3/2/3<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities +2BP<br /> <br /> 5 Melee (specialty swords)<br /> 3 Archery (specialty longbows)<br /> 3 Resistance<br /> 3 Brawl (bare fists)<br /> 3 Investigation (Murders)<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Dodge<br /> 2 Presence<br /> 2 Ride<br /> 2 Integrity<br /> 1 Medicine<br /> 1 Stealth<br /> 1 Socialize<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Wise Arrow<br /> Ferocious Jab<br /> Increasing Strength Exercise<br /> Ten Ox Meditation<br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> One Weapon Two Blows<br /> Dipping Swallow<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> War Lion Stance<br /> 2x Ox Body<br /> Poison Resisting Meditation<br /> Watchman's Infallible Eye<br /> Inquisitor's Unfailing Notice<br /> Crafty Observation Method<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Longbow<br /> Straight Sword<br /> Daiklave<br /> Medium armor hauberk<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Zenith preacher who's goal in life is to spread the good word of his own personal philosophy as gently as he can. He's extremely resistant to having his mind changed about this, and has had to live on his own in the wilderness at times.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Zenith<br /> <br /> Phys<br /> 2/2/4<br /> <br /> Soci<br /> 5/3/3<br /> <br /> Ment<br /> 2/3/2<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities +3bp<br /> <br /> 5 Presence<br /> 4 Integrity<br /> 3 Dodge<br /> 3 Medicine<br /> 3 Performance<br /> 3 Resistance<br /> 2 Survival<br /> 2 Athletics<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Brawl<br /> 2 Socialize<br /> <br /> Charms +12bp<br /> 2x Ox body<br /> Durability of Oak<br /> Spirit Strengthens the Skin<br /> Iron Skin Concentration<br /> Body Mending Meditation<br /> Listener-Swaying Argument<br /> Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> Excellent Friend Approach<br /> Impassioned Discourse Technique<br /> Empowering Shout<br /> Enduring Mental Toughness<br /> Stubborn Boar Defense<br /> Spirit-Maintainint Maneuver<br /> Food-Gathering Exercise<br /> Ailment Rectifying Method<br /> Plague-Banishing Incantation<br /> Wound Mending Care Technique<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Simple precher robes<br /> Mendicant staff<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Twilight sorceress who's life is her books and her places of study. She deftly manages her way around bureaucracies both to manage money and to get at even juicier morsels of knowledge. She's also not above picking the odd easy lock or sneaking around to get it either.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Twilight<br /> <br /> Phys<br /> 2/3/2<br /> <br /> Soci<br /> 3/3/3<br /> <br /> Ment<br /> 3/5/3<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> <br /> 5 Occult<br /> 4 Lore<br /> 3 Linguistics<br /> 3 Dodge<br /> 3 Bureaucracy<br /> 3 Integrity<br /> 2 Stealth<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Larceny<br /> 2 Resistance<br /> 1 Thrown<br /> 1 Larceny<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Sorcery- DoOB<br /> Cirus Skiff<br /> Infallable Messenger<br /> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze<br /> Impervious Sphere of Water<br /> Ancient Tongue Understanding<br /> Supernal Control Method<br /> Spirit-Detecting Glance<br /> Spirit Cutting Attack<br /> Spirit Repelling Diagram<br /> Harmonious Academic Methodology<br /> First Knowledge's Grace<br /> Flowing Mind Prana<br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Drifting Leaf Elusion<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Night caste pure thief, who makes her living, and her fun, out of roaming the rooftops of her home town, slipping silently around, picking pockets and dresser drawers. Often needing to make a quick escape on horseback.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Night<br /> <br /> Phys<br /> 3/3/3<br /> <br /> Soci<br /> 2/3/2<br /> <br /> Ment +4bp<br /> 4/2/4<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities +2bp<br /> <br /> 4 Stealth<br /> 4 Larceny<br /> 3 Awareness<br /> 3 Ride<br /> 3 Dodge<br /> 3 Athletics<br /> 2 Socialize<br /> 2 Investigation<br /> 2 Linguistics<br /> 2 Thrown<br /> 2 Melee<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Excellent Strike<br /> One weapon Two Blows<br /> Precision of the Striking Raptor<br /> Perfect Shadow Stillness<br /> Invisible Statue Spirit<br /> Easily Overlooked Presense Methodology<br /> Blurred Form Style<br /> Seasoned Criminal Method<br /> Clever Bandit's Rook<br /> Flawless Pickpocket Technique<br /> Lock Opening Touch<br /> Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise<br /> Graceful Crane Stance<br /> Monkey Leap Technique<br /> Soaring Crane Leap<br /> <br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> <br /> Enchanted endless bandolier of knives<br /> light armor<br /> thief's tools<br /> Trusty steed<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Eclipse far traveler who wants nothing more or less than to see every single place in the whole world. With a powerful ocean-going ship, a sturdy and swift horse, a knack for languages, and the social skills to fit in anywhere she might actually have what it takes to do that.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Eclipse<br /> <br /> Phys +4bp<br /> 4/4/4<br /> <br /> Soci +3bp<br /> 3/3/2<br /> <br /> Ment +4bp<br /> 4/2/4<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities +4bp<br /> <br /> 5 Sail<br /> 4 Ride<br /> 4 Linguistics<br /> 3 Survival<br /> 3 Lore<br /> 3 Archery<br /> 3 Dodge<br /> 3 Socailize<br /> 2 Resistance<br /> 2 performance<br /> <br /> Charms +4bp<br /> Mastery of Small Manners<br /> Master Horseman's Techniques<br /> Flashing Thunderbolt Steed<br /> Elusive Mount Technique<br /> Wind-Racing Essence Infusion<br /> Salty Dog Method<br /> Shipwreck Surviving Stamina<br /> Fathoms Fed Spirit<br /> Immortal Mariner's Advantage<br /> Legendary Captain's Signature<br /> Wise Arrow<br /> Sight Without Eyes<br /> Reed in the Wind<br /> Reflex Sidestep Technique<br /> Leaping Dodge Method<br /> Strange Tongue Understanding<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Blue Water Merchant yacht<br /> Thoroughbred horse<br /> Magical black jade light armor<br /> shortbow<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Those are not blatantly stupid ways to build your characters, like it's not like an int 7 wizard in DnD. The Dawn is pretty fighty, but also not just focusing on melee, being able to use almost any weapon in the world to kill people, and everyone else has the odd ability to defend themselves, but their real serious focus in on what their character can do with regards to their caste archetype. The preacher doesn't have 5 brawl because he doesn't devote his life to kicking the crap out of people, he's pretty good at it, but his medicine and social skills are top-notch. They're what his character actually focuses on.<br /> <br /> It's really easy to fill out a complete character and after you pick all the cool things you want them to do realize that you kinda forgot to make them a badass in combat. Unfortunately, and I think the system is partially to blame here, and certainly because there's no guidance that you should avoid this especially, people tend to just use 10% of their chargen resources to make themselves an invincible badass and then go on to do what they actually want with their character.<br /> <br /> The game and antagonists play <i>much </i>better with a circle more like I have shown here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T00:09:25-07:00","id":1392136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392035#post1392035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my PCs... iirc, they generally had 3-5 dots in Dexterity, 5 dots in their chosen combat skill, and 4-6 combat Charms-- all dead easy to do at character creation, while leaving more than enough room for their primary specialties. I suggested those as a guideline, to make sure that no-one wound up underpowered and sidelined during combat scenes that could take two hours of table time to play out. If &amp;quot;a third of your starting resources to combat&amp;quot; is beyond the limit of what the system expects to handle, I'd argue that's an issue with the system, not my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rating of 3 is exceptional and 5 is the best in the world. The Corebook suggests 2-5 combat charms, including Ox-body Techniques.<br /> <br /> You advised a group of the most powerful Exalted in the world to be the best in the world at combat. You then advised them to over-spec their Charms to &quot;terrifying assassin&quot; level.<br /> <br /> That Exalted allows you to casually make your bookish nerd the world feather-weight boxing champion is less of an &quot;issue&quot; than a &quot;feature&quot;. If you want to play a game where you steamroll Directional War Gods as OP Warrior-Kings then Exalted lets you do that. But that's not what Volfer and Mirror Flag are doing.<br /> <br /> And the malus here is that you let your Warrior-Kings outnumber their enemies to boot.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I like your solution of only playing with two players. I think that's a great idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392043#post1392043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not counting Reed in the Wind, Drifting Leaf Elusion, Reflex Sidestep Technique, Ox-Body Technique, Blinding Battle Feint, and Stalking Wolf Attitude as combat charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Half and half?<br /> <br /> Like, the Corebook tells you to take 2-5 combat Charms including at least 1 Ox-body Technique. But none of those Charms are from Combat Abilities.<br /> <br /> But sure, if your primary focus is combat, then take 8 combat Charms from at least three different abilities, no more than 3 from Melee.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've discussed this at length before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T00:42:38-07:00","id":1392141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392136#post1392136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Half and half?<br /> <br /> Like, the Corebook tells you to take 2-5 combat Charms including at least 1 Ox-body Technique. But none of those Charms are from Combat Abilities.<br /> <br /> But sure, if your primary focus is combat, then take 8 combat Charms from at least three different abilities, no more than 3 from Melee.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've discussed this at length before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is rather that you present the &quot;frightening assassin&quot; as having 2 Combat Charms, when he actually has 6 more defensive tools that are to be used almost exclusively during combat. I think that present your point in a biased way, which is fine, but without presenting the bias, which has thus been noticed by habitableexoplanet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T03:07:17-07:00","id":1392162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392136#post1392136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me wrong, I like your solution of only playing with two players. I think that's a great idea.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. My personal experience has been 2-3 players plus the ST is the sweet spot in terms of fun, time and having the setting's default challenges make sense. I am in awe of the people here who clearly run great games with more PCs than that.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Are the number of charms so much an issue for people here as the 'passive' advantages most players (including myself) end up taking at chargen because you have <i>so many</i> dots to spend?<br /> <br /> Dex 3+, Combat Ability 5, Specialty (weapon you always use), artefact weapon or armour plus an Excellency quickly renders things other than large numbers or boss fights very easy for, say, an Eclipse who has potentially spent just 2 bonus points, even before you start getting to the charms that make intended default fun opponents trivial.<br /> <br /> Guess it's about having the discipline/wherewithal to build characters like the published examples or DrLoveMonkey's circle above. The above (really cool) Zenith has quite a lot of combat charms by the standards discussed but isn't any great shakes in a fight really, maxes out at a 10-die attack with a one-point stunt and can stack 4 more on top of that if they burn motes. The QC Young Dynast (does anyone still use her?) is a real threat to them.<br /> <br /> As said by others many times before, having slightly lower charm pre-reqs might help with this. Charm trees outside Lunars seem to hit 5s quite quickly.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I've day-dreamed before about 'career skill package suggestions' that detail what you'd expect say, a common soldier, a fisherman or a village shaman to know would inform players better what they should aim for unless they've got reasons not to, a la the Dynast education package from 2e. (I'd add I instinctively have far less isues with Dynasts/Lookshyans/Prasadis etc having 5 in skills at chargen, exceptional education facilities/trained from birth/established heroes etc.)<br /> <br /> QCs - while a good thing overall for my money - and dice pool suggestions don't help inexperienced players visualise what one of the above would know in terms of both <i>breadth</i> and depth of skills (should everyone unless you're a hermit have min Socialise 1? Should everyone except hardened city dwellers have Ride 1?). I've found showing people 2e profiles or Adversaries of the Righteous pdfs is important in those instances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-28-2020, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T03:29:55-07:00","id":1392169,"title":"","content":"I certainly find, for Solars, the main issue is how easy it is to get massive scores, and how the system basically pushes you to do so, and punishes you for not doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I have not found this to be an issue with Lunars, because a lot of it is simply down to freebies, specifically the fact you can get 5 dots in a favoured ability for 2 freebies, which means you can get 7 abilities at 5 (which is probably enough to cover most of what your PC is going to be rolling a lot, if you stick to your niche).<br /> <br /> Whereas with Lunars, you probably have 5 in your favourite attribute (as a Solar probably does anyway), maybe a couple, and then 3s and 4s. Overall, you can roll decent dice pools in lots of areas. But because it costs 2 freebies to get an Ability to 5, and you don't need them for charms anyway, they're much less appealing/encouraged/pushed.<br /> <br /> Of my 6 Lunar PCs, at character creation across all of them there were three Abilities at 5 (only one was a combat ability), and two Abilities at 4. Across 6 characters. Now they're at 100xp, several have spent xp to get a few abilities to 4, but that's it.<br /> So, they can generally roll good dice pools for most things, but are rarely rolling huge dice pools except when stunting and burning 10 motes on an excellency, which they don't do a lot.<br /> <br /> Whereas Solars tend to roll massive dice pools for their focused areas (which on about 80% of characters tends to include combat, even if they don't have a lot of charms for combat), and rubbish dice pools for other stuff, which is more difficult for an ST to run.<br /> <br /> (This is one of the reasons I'm running an all-Lunar game, tbh. They discourage rather than encourage min-maxing, and I find it makes for a more fun and easier to run game.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T05:38:22-07:00","id":1392172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392162#post1392162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the number of charms so much an issue for people here as the 'passive' advantages most players (including myself) end up taking at chargen because you have <i>so many</i> dots to spend?<br /> <br /> Dex 3+, Combat Ability 5, Specialty (weapon you always use), artefact weapon or armour plus an Excellency quickly renders things other than large numbers or boss fights very easy for, say, an Eclipse who has potentially spent just 2 bonus points, even before you start getting to the charms that make intended default fun opponents trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite agree with you. I find some Charms are not really useful. Excellent strike is really good once you have a huge dice pool. But if you have huge dice pool, you likely got a very good fighter already. And if you have a low dice pool, the Charm is not very interesting (saves you some mote, gives you maybe a half success). I mean if you don't intend to make a fighter but just an Eclipse that has something to do in fights, you just use 3 ability points and 2 bp to be on top, and I'll use my Charms for something more useful (maybe 1-2 Ox Body can be useful to be more resilient) like bureaucracy or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:47:26-07:00","id":1392183,"title":"","content":"Yeah, definitely. Non-combat Solars tend to have very high combat dice pools but hardly any combat charms beyond the excellency, and as they have very little else to spend motes in combat on, they throw out big excellencies on all their rolls/defences.<br /> <br /> This isn't always the case, but I find it to be the case 80% of the time. When it's not, it's a deliberate choice.<br /> I deliberately played a character with Dex 2 and 1 dot of Brawl, who then learnt Martial Arts up to 5 over the campaign as a character arc, and that was kind of fun, but even considering that our ST tends to throw very easy combat encounters at us (well, for our level), he was a total chump at combat compared to his companions. And that's why he lost an arm, an eye and several toes. It would have cost very little in the way of starting resources to be way, way better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-28-2020, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:00:08-07:00","id":1392192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392118#post1392118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do agree that it's a problem, but it is also possible to make characters like this</div> </div> </div> </div>True... but it's also an argument that feels really familiar to someone who spent a lot of time arguing about 3.5e D&amp;D imbalances-- &quot;this isn't a mechanical problem because I can make the deliberate informed choice to avoid it.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392136#post1392136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Corebook suggests 2-5 combat charms, including Ox-body Techniques... You advised a group of the most powerful Exalted in the world to be the best in the world at combat. You then advised them to over-spec their Charms to &quot;terrifying assassin&quot; level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, the book says &quot;Generally, 2-5 combat Charms should be sufficient to keep your Solar from dying at the hands of the first bandit gang to come along and permit her to stand up in the face of basic supernatural opposition.&quot; <i>Basic </i>supernatural opposition. I don't know about you, but that suggests 5 combat Charms makes for a generally capable mid-range combatant, not an OP Warrior-King.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the example character, the &quot;terrifying assassin.&quot; According to the text, the player's intention is to make him &quot;good at sneaking around and killing, as well as <i>competent </i>in a straight-up fight (emphasis mine). At the end of the process, he has Dex 5, Melee 4, a Melee specialty, a third of his Merit points spent on combat traits, and 6 combat Charms (8 if you count Blinding Battle Feint and Stalking Wolf Attitude). This is identified as a &quot;stealth-based fighter--an unusual approach.&quot; Not a master martial artist, not a samurai champion, not a barbarian warlord. There is, in fact, <i>nothing </i>to suggest that Otso's 2 attack, 3 dodge, and 1 resistance Charm will make him into a creation-shaking warrior god. Can you really blame me for pointing my players to similar spreads?<br /> <br /> But look-- the problem I've run into isn't in the power of individual Solars. Hell, just yesterday, I was testing a potential houserule by running a Fair Folk Cataphract against a fresh Solar with very similar stats to Otso (Dex 5, Martial Arts 5, and 5 combat Charms-- 2 offensive, 2 defensive, 1 dual-role) and ran him with 30m to simulate a character who'd done some stuff before fighting. And it was a real fight, and if I'd continued for more than a few rounds it might have been a losing one. My guy smacked the Cataphract a couple times with Motion of Myriad Legs for some real pain, but burned through his motes real fast trying to keep up with his foe's 16d to attack and Parry 7. After three rounds, I was down to the 5m/turn mote regeneration and the Fae still had most of his health levels left.<br /> <br /> The problem is that three copies of my character verses that same Cataphract make mincemeat out of him without being scratched. That five copies can splatter Ahlat without feeling pressured. That's not an issue with character power; that's an issue with a system that assumes a fairly large number of players (a five-Solar circle) will generally be outnumbered by foes with real mechanical complexity... and without offering so much as a scrap of advice hinting at that or suggesting ways to build significant encounters.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> (That all said: I do very much want to try running Ex3 again with a better understanding of how encounters are supposed to flow and better houserules/techniques to streamline combat. And without a defense-optimized character focused around War Lion Stance and a misunderstanding of Defend Other rules in my group.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:14:11-07:00","id":1392196,"title":"","content":"So don't fight 3 PCs vs 1 Cataphract?<br /> <br /> Have a battlegroup of hobgoblins (Might 1, handwave the Charms), the Cat (complex combat character), and a Lorelei (no combat charms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:41:46-07:00","id":1392210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392136#post1392136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half and half?<br /> <br /> Like, the Corebook tells you to take 2-5 combat Charms including at least 1 Ox-body Technique. But none of those Charms are from Combat Abilities.<br /> <br /> But sure, if your primary focus is combat, then take 8 combat Charms from at least three different abilities, no more than 3 from Melee.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I've discussed this at length before.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have, and I agree with your main points that (a) players will have more fun if their characters are not super powerful in combat, (b) the system is designed around this, (c) it's good that the system gives you ways to be super powerful in combat despite this. I disagree with a couple things:<br /> <br /> (1) I don't think the example in the corebook alone is a sufficient explanation of how and why to design characters not overspecced for combat. (I agree that Tomb of Dreams helps though.)<br /> <br /> (2) I think you're presenting the issue in a strange way in that post by focusing on Charms in the main combat Ability rather than other features of character power. (I think you did a very good job presenting the issue in many previous posts.) In particular, the book character is weaker than typical naive PCs in part because he has so many Charms (and therefore fewer bonus points to spend on Abilities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392162#post1392162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the number of charms so much an issue for people here as the 'passive' advantages most players (including myself) end up taking at chargen because you have <i>so many</i> dots to spend?<br /> <br /> Dex 3+, Combat Ability 5, Specialty (weapon you always use), artefact weapon or armour plus an Excellency quickly renders things other than large numbers or boss fights very easy for, say, an Eclipse who has potentially spent just 2 bonus points, even before you start getting to the charms that make intended default fun opponents trivial.<br /> <br /> Guess it's about having the discipline/wherewithal to build characters like the published examples or DrLoveMonkey's circle above. The above (really cool) Zenith has quite a lot of combat charms by the standards discussed but isn't any great shakes in a fight really, maxes out at a 10-die attack with a one-point stunt and can stack 4 more on top of that if they burn motes. The QC Young Dynast (does anyone still use her?) is a real threat to them.<br /> <br /> As said by others many times before, having slightly lower charm pre-reqs might help with this. Charm trees outside Lunars seem to hit 5s quite quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this point of view. It takes real effort while building many characters to find cool things to spend dots on without doing too well at combat.<br /> <br /> One can avoid getting Artifacts and just spend the Merit dots on something else, but some of the other things to spend Merit dots on, like Command, Familiar, and Retainers, can also make combat worse. (The trick the corebook character uses is to take a lot of the relatively unexciting purchased Merits that give you +1 to something, instead of the more dangerous Merits.)<br /> <br /> I especially agree with the idea that charm pre-reqs could be a little lower. In particular, while playing around with the character creation, I have found Martial Arts (especially social-focused ones like Dreaming Pearl Courtesan) to be a great way to:<ul><li>Pick enough combat Charms to have things to do in combat</li> <li>Not have a reason to take more than 2-5 combat Charms (because that's all that's available at Essence 1)</li> <li>Have unique abilities in combat (instead of taking 2 Melee Charms and playing with a Dawn who has all the same Charms plus two more)</li> <li>Fit a noncombat-focused character's concept</li> <li>Spend Merit dots (on the Martial Artist Merit)</li> </ul>However, some Martial Arts have the Form charm at Martial Arts 4, Essence 1 which has a cool theme that is super tempting but if you take that, your Ability rating will be almost the maximum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392192#post1392192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And without a defense-optimized character focused around War Lion Stance and a misunderstanding of Defend Other rules in my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the story here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392196#post1392196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So don't fight 3 PCs vs 1 Cataphract?<br /> <br /> Have a battlegroup of hobgoblins (Might 1, handwave the Charms), the Cat (complex combat character), and a Lorelei (no combat charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>I in particular second the Lorelei recommendation, whose low defenses combined with ability to drain the PC's Willpower make the players feel both powerful and endangered while also not making combat go on very long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:25:02-07:00","id":1392266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392210#post1392210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, while playing around with the character creation, I have found Martial Arts (especially social-focused ones like Dreaming Pearl Courtesan) to be a great way to:</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Taking the first couple Evocations of an artifact isn't bad either, if you grab one like the Distaff that has enough Essence 1 options.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the story here? </div> </div> </div>Ugh. The character was built to do two things: craft and tank. He took a supernatural Merit (representing mutations from an alchemical accident) to bump his base soak, wore heavy armor, and crafted himself Irenio\u2019s Bell (which, for the record, I feel like has much too powerful a base effect for a three-dot artifact, but I digress). In combat, he'd usually spend his actions on Full Defense, then use War Lion Stance every time anyone in the circle was attacked. This was partly aided by my allowing a generous interpretation of &quot;close range,&quot; but mostly because we both missed the rule that if you beat the guardian's parry, you can choose to apply your attack directly to them rather than keep going at the ward using only threshold successes. Which, uh... in retrospect may have been a much bigger factor in my difficulties than I realized before I started typing this out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> (He also wanted to Craft his way around every issue, with extremely generous assumptions about how long projects would take. It also forced <i>me </i>to write a lot of custom mechanics and Evocations because his character could pump out artifacts for everyone in the party, and the one time I let him do it the proposal was insanely overpowered)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 05-28-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:28:48-07:00","id":1392267,"title":"","content":"That is a fairly big factor, but if he had a ton of soak its still a strong tactic. Does mean he's going to take a lot of decisives though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:30:33-07:00","id":1392275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392162#post1392162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess it's about having the discipline/wherewithal to build characters like the published examples or DrLoveMonkey's circle above. The above (really cool) Zenith has quite a lot of combat charms by the standards discussed but isn't any great shakes in a fight really, maxes out at a 10-die attack with a one-point stunt and can stack 4 more on top of that if they burn motes. The QC Young Dynast (does anyone still use her?) is a real threat to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392210#post1392210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this point of view. It takes real effort while building many characters to find cool things to spend dots on without doing too well at combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I somewhat disagree on this. It only really takes real effort to avoid making a combat monster in avoiding the temptation to do so. There's way more non-combat charms and merits than there are combat ones. If you just take mostly abilities and charms from:<br /> <br /> Athletics -barring a couple like Thunderbolt Attack Prana<br /> Awareness<br /> Bureaucracy<br /> Craft<br /> Integrity<br /> Investigation<br /> Larceny<br /> Linguistics<br /> Lore<br /> Medicine<br /> Occult<br /> Performance<br /> Presence<br /> Ride - barring some stuff for mounted combat<br /> Sail - barring naval combat<br /> Socialize<br /> Stealth<br /> Survival - barring supernal survival with a tyrant lizard<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you'll be not very good at combat. If you want a strategy on how to do that and not feel bad, first take every non-combat charm and ability you can, until all your points are spent, and then start cutting things out in order to take combat stuff. Even then, consider taking things like Call the Blade/Summoning the Loyal steel. Also spend all your merit points before taking combat artifacts.<br /> <br /> That way you actually have to tell yourself &quot;No, my character does not have the ability to run straight up vertical surfaces like an epic fantasy ninja, I choose to cut that power out in order to take Excellent Strike.&quot; then you go &quot;And, neither does he have the ability to run across water, or up falling lotus leaves as he dashes through the moonlight, instead he has One Weapon Two Blows.&quot; and you might end up saying &quot;Okay, I could take Peony Blossom Attack, but then I don't even have Graceful Crane Stance to let me perfectly balance on ropes or tree branches, and that's really cool so fuck it, Melee 2 and two melee charms are where I'm at.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also consider diversifying your combat ability. If your character is a knife fighter, and you only have melee, you can't do any throwing knife stuff. Also if he's supposed to be a street fighter, what happens when you have no knife, or get disarmed? Brawl 0 makes you worthless in the fight without a weapon, is your character the kind of fighter that surrenders as soon as they get disarmed? If not, get at least a bit of Brawl.<br /> <br /> Likewise look at things like Integrity. Is your character easily swayed? If not, get at least some integrity. Is your character really open for having their intimacies read? If not, get at least some socialize. Does your character have any hobbies like playing an instrument or riding? Well get at least a dot or two there. Is your character even a little bit personable? Probably grab a dot of presence then.<br /> <br /> Of course, two dots in something represents a professional mortal, but at the same time your Solars are not going up against professional mortals. Integrity/socialize 1-2 might be okay if a minor mortal courtier is trying to sway your character, but a Fair Folk Lorelei will read you like a book and have your intimacies as putty in her hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392196#post1392196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So don't fight 3 PCs vs 1 Cataphract?<br /> <br /> Have a battlegroup of hobgoblins (Might 1, handwave the Charms), the Cat (complex combat character), and a Lorelei (no combat charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, and I've said this multiple times but it bears repeating. You will never ever challenge your PCs with one single combat scene. When the Dawn gets to smirk and say &quot;Excuse me while I spend 40m and 5wp in one single turn shafa-KOOOM-psh-whrrrr...&quot; and splatter five enemies before they can even act to draw their weapons, that's it, the fight's over.<br /> <br /> If you're going after a fair folk lord do this:<ul><li>Scene 1 palace gate, with two Cataphracts, and a size 2 battlegroup of hobgoblins. Especially important here to launch low initiative decisive attacks to start wounding people</li> <li>Scene 2 throneroom, the PCs arrive just in time to see the lord slipping into a concealed door behind the throne. The massive throneroom is home to a fake court of Size 3 Battlegroup walking statues, another cataphract, and a lorelei.</li> <li>Scene 2.5 hidden passage door, it takes a difficulty 5 lockpicking roll or a Strength 7, 12 success Feat of Strength.</li> <li>Scene 3 Underground Harbour The lord attempts to flee on his deamship, but he will do battle with his Size 2 battlegroup of minor cataphract knights with Elite drill, and himself who uses the stats of Iolanthe, Queen of the Beryl Palace if confronted. For bonus points have everyone roll a Dexterity + Dodge hazard at the end of every round, difficulty 3 or take 3L dice of damage from falling pieces of crumbling reality crashing down around them. Remembering everyone who didn't take dodge and is wearing heavy armor is making that roll of straight (Dexterity - 2) dice.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> At no point there are you running a combat with more than three Storyteller characters, and never more than two with motepools. It's only three scenes which is relatively short, but you'd still need to be pretty darn optimized in your whole group if you get to that final fight with enough resources left to just clown it. Especially if your characters just get fed up with those battlegroups and blow a ton of motes just to burn them down fast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:51:54-07:00","id":1392284,"title":"","content":"Also if you want to make it even harder, throw in some super critical but quick non-combat scenes. Like maybe the passage leads to a maze of tunnels that you need to do a hard survival tracking test to get through. It takes like two minutes to roll that out, the guy with survival will spend a bunch of motes on it, then you move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T15:56:14-07:00","id":1392343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392275#post1392275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I somewhat disagree on this. It only really takes real effort to avoid making a combat monster in avoiding the temptation to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely probably overstated the case. I don't think if I was making a character for a game right now, I would screw up and accidentally make a combat monster.<br /> <br /> My experience comes only from my first game character and some theoretical game characters. I just had the experience once or twice of intentionally trying to tone down the power level and realizing at the end of character creation that it was too high. <br /> <br /> In a game, I would probably revise and fix this. I'm not saying anyone will come to my house and force me to write Melee 5 on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you'll be not very good at combat. If you want a strategy on how to do that and not feel bad, first take every non-combat charm and ability you can, until all your points are spent, and then start cutting things out in order to take combat stuff. Even then, consider taking things like Call the Blade/Summoning the Loyal steel. Also spend all your merit points before taking combat artifacts. </div> </div> </div>This is a really good idea. (Though the existence of this kind of clever strategy doesn't negate the nontriviality of the problem).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That way you actually have to tell yourself &quot;No, my character does not have the ability to run straight up vertical surfaces like an epic fantasy ninja, I choose to cut that power out in order to take Excellent Strike.&quot; then you go &quot;And, neither does he have the ability to run across water, or up falling lotus leaves as he dashes through the moonlight, instead he has One Weapon Two Blows.&quot; and you might end up saying &quot;Okay, I could take Peony Blossom Attack, but then I don't even have Graceful Crane Stance to let me perfectly balance on ropes or tree branches, and that's really cool so fuck it, Melee 2 and two melee charms are where I'm at.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting point. Like, if I start thinking of a concept for a character who isn't focused on combat, I don't often rush to Abilities like Athletics because character archetypes like &quot;a rich merchant prince&quot; or &quot;a creepy witch who appears out of nowhere&quot; don't usually have that kind of power. But I could, instead of or in addition to going &quot;well, he should probably be able to defend himself&quot;, go &quot;well, he should probably be able to run up walls&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will remember this package any time I'm low on Charms to take for a build.<br /> <br /> But it is a somewhat strange / nonobvious solution to take a bunch of Charms whose main application is combat but aren't as powerful as the main combat Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also consider diversifying your combat ability. If your character is a knife fighter, and you only have melee, you can't do any throwing knife stuff. Also if he's supposed to be a street fighter, what happens when you have no knife, or get disarmed? Brawl 0 makes you worthless in the fight without a weapon, is your character the kind of fighter that surrenders as soon as they get disarmed? If not, get at least a bit of Brawl. </div> </div> </div>I hate this but this is a fair point.<br /> <br /> Ironically the main Exalt type this doesn't apply to are Lunars, thanks to their Attribute-based excellencies (well assuming they have the Dex excellency) but they almost all have Brawl for another reason (fighting in animal forms).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise look at things like Integrity. Is your character easily swayed? If not, get at least some integrity. Is your character really open for having their intimacies read? If not, get at least some socialize. Does your character have any hobbies like playing an instrument or riding? Well get at least a dot or two there. Is your character even a little bit personable? Probably grab a dot of presence then. </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. This is another thing that is somewhat easier in a real game than making theoretical characters - my current character has a dot or two of Sail, which he's never used, because he used to be a pirate. (Although I did go full &quot;Put one dot in everything you can imagine your character doing. Now put two dots in everything they are an expert in. Now put three dots in everything they're really really good at, until you run out of dots.&quot; on my Lunar Batman.) Still it pains me a bit to do this in the official character creation system (not using XP-based character creation.)<br /> <br /> Also fair point about Integrity, and Socialize. (I would lump Resistance in here too because it's not used in typical combat situations). I usually start by thinking of all the cool stuff my character can do and do the defensive stuff last with spare points, but it might be wiser to play a little attention to them. <br /> <br /> I do, at least, remember to put dots into social influence abilities unless the character would never engage in social influence for some reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, two dots in something represents a professional mortal, but at the same time your Solars are not going up against professional mortals. Integrity/socialize 1-2 might be okay if a minor mortal courtier is trying to sway your character, but a Fair Folk Lorelei will read you like a book and have your intimacies as putty in her hands. </div> </div> </div> I recently got Integrity 5 in my high Essence Solar game and still find the Fair Folk Lorelei's dice pool terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T17:03:17-07:00","id":1392359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392343#post1392343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really good idea. (Though the existence of this kind of clever strategy doesn't negate the nontriviality of the problem).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's a strategy to fix a problem, but it also only works if the whole party is on board with doing it too. It's pretty simple psychology, but it works even on yourself. As soon as you frame it as having to give up this cool thing that you've already picked, you're less likely to want to let it go in favour of grabbing combat stuff just because you feel like you need a combat baseline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392343#post1392343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very interesting point. Like, if I start thinking of a concept for a character who isn't focused on combat, I don't often rush to Abilities like Athletics because character archetypes like &quot;a rich merchant prince&quot; or &quot;a creepy witch who appears out of nowhere&quot; don't usually have that kind of power. But I could, instead of or in addition to going &quot;well, he should probably be able to defend himself&quot;, go &quot;well, he should probably be able to run up walls&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and there's a lot of powers like that. A rich merchant prince might just as likely be very good at defending himself as sprinting straight up walls, or look at Flashing Thunderbolt Steed, if he needs to make a fast courier trip, or escape a bad situation, that's very helpful. For a merchant, obviously Bureacuracy is important, but you also don't want people you're making deals with to know all your intimacies, so gotta get socialize. They might guess anyway though, so Integrity is very important. Also what if somebody tries something shifty and poisons your drink at a negotiation? Resistance charms help out there. Also if you're taking your caravan convoy of supplies through the deepest, darkest forests or across the burning sands you need Survival, absolutely.<br /> <br /> Making deals though, that's not just an in person thing, and it's really hard to make deal across language barriers, so Linguistics is top notch to have as well. If you're taking your trade on a boat, or even an airship, sandship, or iceship you're gonna want sail, just in case. If you're worried about crime as well, either against your merchant empire or being facilitated within it, that's something you want Investigation for. Or maybe you want to engage in a bit of that yourself, you know, slight of hand a bill of lading out from under somebody, so that's larceny.<br /> <br /> <br /> For your merits too, you want Contacts, Influence, probably Backing, maybe a retainer, definitely Followers, definitely Languages, and 100% resources. You might even want multiple areas of contacts, for example both within the Guild and among local western leaders. After all of that, try to find 6+ merit dots left for artifact weapon/armor. I honestly even have trouble doing that for DB characters, and they get like 18 merit points.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of that relies on your Storyteller too though. If the only thing he ever has you guys do is just get into a fight, and then you win, and then it's off to the next fight, you're not really going to get to shine bright as a merchant prince like that, and you're better off just making a combat character who has some bureaucracy. On the other hand if you take 10+ dots of Contacts, and any time you say &quot;Do I know a guy who...?&quot; he says &quot;You absolutely know a guy.&quot; then you're very justified in not decking yourself out in magic weapons and armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:07:18-07:00","id":1392371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392359#post1392359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your merits too, you want Contacts, Influence, probably Backing, maybe a retainer, definitely Followers, definitely Languages, and 100% resources. You might even want multiple areas of contacts, for example both within the Guild and among local western leaders. After all of that, try to find 6+ merit dots left for artifact weapon/armor. I honestly even have trouble doing that for DB characters, and they get like 18 merit points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that particular guy wasn't a great example because I didn't have a &quot;too much combat power&quot; problem with him - in part because I took most of the abilities you mention. <br /> <br /> (A fun trick for character creation I learned accidentally by making theoretical characters - come up with 3 different concepts, build each of them, and play whichever one you have the hardest time fitting all the Charms / Merits / other cool stuff into the allotted slots.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of that relies on your Storyteller too though. If the only thing he ever has you guys do is just get into a fight, and then you win, and then it's off to the next fight, you're not really going to get to shine bright as a merchant prince like that, and you're better off just making a combat character who has some bureaucracy. On the other hand if you take 10+ dots of Contacts, and any time you say &quot;Do I know a guy who...?&quot; he says &quot;You absolutely know a guy.&quot; then you're very justified in not decking yourself out in magic weapons and armor. </div> </div> </div>I feel like it also relies on the player a bit too. Like I'm pretty confident that if I take some combat Charms and I'm in a combat scene then I will remember to use my combat Charms. But if I've not played a game / character like that before, I'm not necessarily going to think &quot;What skills or resources would I need to deal with this problem, and how likely would my Contacts be to have those skills or resources?&quot; instead of &quot;How can I deal with this problem myself?&quot;. So I understand why people might be more confident that combat powers will be useful to them than other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T00:21:52-07:00","id":1392430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392275#post1392275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going after a fair folk lord do this:<ul><li>Scene 1 palace gate, with two Cataphracts, and a size 2 battlegroup of hobgoblins. Especially important here to launch low initiative decisive attacks to start wounding people</li> <li>Scene 2 throneroom, the PCs arrive just in time to see the lord slipping into a concealed door behind the throne. The massive throneroom is home to a fake court of Size 3 Battlegroup walking statues, another cataphract, and a lorelei.</li> <li>Scene 2.5 hidden passage door, it takes a difficulty 5 lockpicking roll or a Strength 7, 12 success Feat of Strength.</li> <li>Scene 3 Underground Harbour The lord attempts to flee on his deamship, but he will do battle with his Size 2 battlegroup of minor cataphract knights with Elite drill, and himself who uses the stats of Iolanthe, Queen of the Beryl Palace if confronted. For bonus points have everyone roll a Dexterity + Dodge hazard at the end of every round, difficulty 3 or take 3L dice of damage from falling pieces of crumbling reality crashing down around them. Remembering everyone who didn't take dodge and is wearing heavy armor is making that roll of straight (Dexterity - 2) dice.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> At no point there are you running a combat with more than three Storyteller characters, and never more than two with motepools. It's only three scenes which is relatively short, but you'd still need to be pretty darn optimized in your whole group if you get to that final fight with enough resources left to just clown it. Especially if your characters just get fed up with those battlegroups and blow a ton of motes just to burn them down fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree quite a bit with you about one specific thing : I think combat is long in Exalted, even when it's supposed to be simple, and that makes a long 3 combat session with 2 of them are narratively not &quot;interesting&quot; (except if the player had some prior emotional stakes with the guarding cataphracts or the Lorelei). <br /> <br /> However, if the Crucible's Legends have rules for quick combat at someone mentioned in the dedicated thread, I think your solution is the go-to that most people don't think to do (me included).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:23:19-07:00","id":1392457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392371#post1392371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (A fun trick for character creation I learned accidentally by making theoretical characters - come up with 3 different concepts, build each of them, and play whichever one you have the hardest time fitting all the Charms / Merits / other cool stuff into the allotted slots.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea; a lot of concepts can be made with less dots than you get, so then you tend to throw extra stuff on and dilute the concept (plus experience over the game). So I can see the value in this idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:36:02-07:00","id":1392458,"title":"","content":"I should say that combat between a battlegroup and PCs is quick, but I'd think the 2 cataphracts as well would make it take much longer. Though it really depends on the PCs and the player's play style. Big alpha strikes make combat quick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of interest, how often do you guys have combats? I normally have a small combat every... 2 sessions on average? Like some first circle demons or a gribbly monster or a couple of Dragonblood. And then a serious combat with a battle group and some Dragonblood, or a huge spirit monster, or something like that, every 4-5 sessions I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:02:07-07:00","id":1392463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392458#post1392458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should say that combat between a battlegroup and PCs is quick, but I'd think the 2 cataphracts as well would make it take much longer. Though it really depends on the PCs and the player's play style. Big alpha strikes make combat quick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of interest, how often do you guys have combats? I normally have a small combat every... 2 sessions on average? Like some first circle demons or a gribbly monster or a couple of Dragonblood. And then a serious combat with a battle group and some Dragonblood, or a huge spirit monster, or something like that, every 4-5 sessions I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say usually the same, maybe a bit more often. Really huge titanesque combat are at the same rhythm, but I try to put some minor ennemies once every session to keep the &quot;dangerous&quot; Exalted world feature.<br /> <br /> Yeah against a battlegroup only it could go fast, but I expect 2 cataphracts and 1 battlegroup size 2 should take a bit more time. If they are not narratively relevant, I'm afraid with the actual combat system it might take too long for what it's worth. Depending on the number of players you have also, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:10:49-07:00","id":1392465,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'm not sure I've ever actually used a Cataphract against PCs (they actually made friends with the ice-Raksha in my game, so didn't really fight them, just a bit of wrestling ice-gians).<br /> So I'm not really sure how they play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:35:30-07:00","id":1392470,"title":"","content":"I don't know either but each are 18hp. If you have a team of 3 PC it might take some time, especially if you want to exhaust them in the long run. If it was a simple unique fight I wouldn't worry anything over it. With 5 PC's I think it should be effective but still long, that's why I have high hopes for the Crucible's Legends and potential fast fighting sub-system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:07:58-07:00","id":1392487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392470#post1392470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know either but each are 18hp. If you have a team of 3 PC it might take some time, especially if you want to exhaust them in the long run. If it was a simple unique fight I wouldn't worry anything over it. With 5 PC's I think it should be effective but still long, that's why I have high hopes for the Crucible's Legends and potential fast fighting sub-system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have definitely found the long health tracks of Cataphracts to take a long time to deal with.<br /> I've also found that, once the PCs have gotten wound levels on/gotten ride of battlegroups/killed one of the cataphracts, it's possible for the fight to take along time without being challenging, and it's possible to be gaining more motes than you spend while wearing the Cataphract down, which can diminish the effectiveness of Cataphracts as an opening fight.<br /> <br /> Both of which are why I've started declaring fights over well before the Cataphracts actually die, which I've found to work fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:15:36-07:00","id":1392491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392430#post1392430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to disagree quite a bit with you about one specific thing : I think combat is long in Exalted, even when it's supposed to be simple, and that makes a long 3 combat session with 2 of them are narratively not &amp;quot;interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>I also made up that list of scenes with the idea that the storyteller running them has been experiencing players absolutely blast through enemies with no contest. If they\u2019re really really powerful they could easily take out the first two combats in one round each. For smaller groups or less powerful ones that might be excessive.<br /> <br /> I do think there\u2019s good reasons to do it though, just as long as the combats aren\u2019t too similar. Like I wouldn\u2019t have a throne room combat, and then right after that another hidden throne room with the exact same enemies. Having one at the gatehouse which is super fast, and then one inside the throne room with different enemies and maybe the wafting scent of enchanted food causing complications or something, and then another in an underground crumbling cavern might be okay.<br /> <br /> One reason is it lets the players have their cake and eat it too as far as their characters are concerned. If they\u2019re playing Solars and they built their Solars to be as strong as they could, they should really feel strong, like very very strong. So if you\u2019re way stronger than any one enemy you face, you get to feel that way. It\u2019s just that at that point the only time you feel any pressure is if you\u2019re outnumbered, often greatly.<br /> <br /> But also running 9 NPCs in a single combat is a horrible headache. So that\u2019s where splitting them up into multiple fights comes into it. Really it doesn\u2019t even have to be three fights, I just put that because we were talking about combat. It could be two fights, a chaos-puzzle door, a social encounter, an environmental hazard, and a chase scene. That really feels a lot more like an adventure to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392458#post1392458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should say that combat between a battlegroup and PCs is quick, but I'd think the 2 cataphracts as well would make it take much longer. Though it really depends on the PCs and the player's play style. Big alpha strikes make combat quick.<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of interest, how often do you guys have combats? I normally have a small combat every... 2 sessions on average? Like some first circle demons or a gribbly monster or a couple of Dragonblood. And then a serious combat with a battle group and some Dragonblood, or a huge spirit monster, or something like that, every 4-5 sessions I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It varies a lot, and also different campaigns are different. There might be a really fast combat in most sessions, but a lot of the time it\u2019s not one we bust out the combat system for, it\u2019s just one to skip. Or maybe one we do bust out the system for but it\u2019s over in a round. Then every other session, or once every three maybe there\u2019s some actual serious stuff going down that might make for a bigger combat, or multiples, or a combat set into so many other things that it feels big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:19:23-07:00","id":1392493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392487#post1392487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of which are why I've started declaring fights over well before the Cataphracts actually die, which I've found to work fairly well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is that a good strategy, but in 90% of combats it probably makes a ton of sense. If a Dawn just flashed gold and killed 10 of the best soldiers I\u2019ve ever seen, and then levels their blade on me, I\u2019m running, or surrendering. You need to be extremely brave combined with a great reason to fight to the end not to do that. Also in-combat note regen is supposed to come from the adrenaline overdrive of deadly combat, which I have to assume goes away once you\u2019ve basically won the fight against a wounded single opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:10:12-07:00","id":1392508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392430#post1392430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to disagree quite a bit with you about one specific thing : I think combat is long in Exalted, even when it's supposed to be simple, and that makes a long 3 combat session with 2 of them are narratively not &quot;interesting&quot; (except if the player had some prior emotional stakes with the guarding cataphracts or the Lorelei).<br /> <br /> However, if the Crucible's Legends have rules for quick combat at someone mentioned in the dedicated thread, I think your solution is the go-to that most people don't think to do (me included).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to agree with this-- when combat takes a long time, &quot;multiple combats over the course of the day&quot; becomes a lot more tedious, even if you <i>do </i>switch to narrative mode once the fight is basically won (which honestly is good advice for all RPGs). I'm starting to gear up for a new attempt at running Ex3, and quick combat resolution rules are definitely going on my list of things to prepare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:14:16-07:00","id":1392513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392508#post1392508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got to agree with this-- when combat takes a long time, &amp;quot;multiple combats over the course of the day&amp;quot; becomes a lot more tedious, even if you <i>do </i>switch to narrative mode once the fight is basically won (which honestly is good advice for all RPGs). I'm starting to gear up for a new attempt at running Ex3, and quick combat resolution rules are definitely going on my list of things to prepare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, how much actual time and how many rounds would you expect a fight against two Cataphracts and a battlegroup to go? With some groups I\u2019ve run it would take two rounds and maybe a half hour out of a 3-5 hour session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:30:53-07:00","id":1392518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392513#post1392513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, how much actual time and how many rounds would you expect a fight against two Cataphracts and a battlegroup to go? With some groups I\u2019ve run it would take two rounds and maybe a half hour out of a 3-5 hour session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has more to do with deploying all the &quot;combat&quot; arsenal (prepare Initiative, possibly prepare a battle map, let players prepare their followers and whatnot, etc ...) all this just to make an alpha strike turn 1 where the ennemies are apparently so crippled after that they can't even play ... I'd just really rather make this either only 1 roll from the player part, or just prepare one unique big battle.<br /> <br /> I feel the system is not really adapted to make &quot;skirmishes&quot; or quick fights right now, it's not just about the time it takes, it's also about the mentality and preparation that goes along with it.<br /> <br /> But if you want my honest answer, I think with my usual players it could go easily 3/4 of an hour or 1 whole hour if some player decided to have some crazy idea (rally the Cataphract against the big bad fey or whatever), which is a bit much is then we have to do another fight in the palace and then again a last boss fight. If I could likely do the first 2 fights in 45 mns total though, I'd be very much inclined to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:43:47-07:00","id":1392525,"title":"","content":"Ah okay, my group doesn\u2019t tend to use battle maps for exalted, or if we do it\u2019s something drawn in ten to fifteen seconds to show there\u2019s a gate, a drawbridge and a crumbling tower. I also have an agreement with my players that they won\u2019t bog down the game with followers. Followers and retainers and stuff you can have Pretty much one of them roll into combat with you If you are not super combat savvy yourself, but otherwise their use is for being places you can\u2019t, guarding you while you sleep, etc. <br /> <br /> We also roll up pretty fast, we\u2019ve got a number line kind of grid with little wooden tiles that have our names on them, so everyone just rolls their initiative and puts their tiles into place themselves. It takes longer than setting up in DnD, but not too much longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:10:04-07:00","id":1392538,"title":"","content":"Playing only online with dicebots and using LCA's combat tracker shaves down some delay factors in my experience. The dicebots cut out most of the delays in rolling (counting up your dice, applying dicetricks by hand, counting up successes), and LCA makes keeping track of all your bits and bobs take less time as well.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't really go to the full system for quick skirmishes either, and quick combat is something I agree with. I'm in a game in which we had a fighting tournament that was all NPCs and one PC, and for each fight we did a simple roll-off---including the ones where the PC was in the ring.<br /> <br /> You could even use a quick roll-off system for fights where it's not really a question of whether the PCs win, but instead a question of &quot;how cleanly&quot; or &quot;how quickly&quot; or &quot;how impressively&quot; or whatever, depending on what's at stake in the narrative. That kind of makes more sense to me in some situations than actually having the roll-off determine whether the PCs win at all, if it's a case where you can reasonably project that they'd probably win one way or another. If your fightstick Dawn rolls off against a schlubby mortal guard to try to knock him out quickly and happens to lose that roll, it seems a little goofy if somehow that guard kicks the Dawn's ass---if you played that fight out for real, it is highly unlikely that the mortal would be able to win. Instead I'd have that failure mean the guard is able to alert others before he's KO'd, or he manages to scramble away, or even that the Dawn accidentally kills him rather than just knocking him out (though this is only for if the killing is a significantly suboptimal result in your scenario).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:02:52-07:00","id":1392582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392513#post1392513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, how much actual time and how many rounds would you expect a fight against two Cataphracts and a battlegroup to go? With some groups I\u2019ve run it would take two rounds and maybe a half hour out of a 3-5 hour session.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the 4-5 person group I had? Two hours, easy. We played ~3 hours once a week; the longest fight (four Solars against three war gods in a complex arena) took two straight sessions.<br /> <br /> For quick combat, I'm wondering about something along the lines of: &quot;everyone rolls Dex+Combat skill, and each side adds their successes together.&quot;<ul><li>If the players win, they're good--they kick their foes' asses with no more resource expenditure than they dumped into the initial roll. That represents a fight where they just steamroller everything.</li> <li>If the players lose, they have to buy off the difference-- for every success the foe beats them by, the group (collectively) has to spend 1 health level <i>or </i>1wp <i>or </i>5m. (Or something of that nature, like a point of Size of an battle group or the death of a minor ally), That represents a fight significant enough that it involved some danger and resource drain. (They could also just accept the loss and take the consequences, of course).</li> </ul><br /> That gives you a fairly fast resolution that involves the whole group and focuses in on the actual question asked by chaff fights-- not &quot;did anyone get hurt,&quot; but rather &quot;how many resources did we burn?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:54:54-07:00","id":1392615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392525#post1392525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah okay, my group doesn\u2019t tend to use battle maps for exalted, or if we do it\u2019s something drawn in ten to fifteen seconds to show there\u2019s a gate, a drawbridge and a crumbling tower. I also have an agreement with my players that they won\u2019t bog down the game with followers. Followers and retainers and stuff you can have Pretty much one of them roll into combat with you If you are not super combat savvy yourself, but otherwise their use is for being places you can\u2019t, guarding you while you sleep, etc.<br /> <br /> We also roll up pretty fast, we\u2019ve got a number line kind of grid with little wooden tiles that have our names on them, so everyone just rolls their initiative and puts their tiles into place themselves. It takes longer than setting up in DnD, but not too much longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think your group is much better organized that the players I'm used to. I think I would gain imposing some stricter rules at my tables concerning Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:29:53-07:00","id":1392703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392615#post1392615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think your group is much better organized that the players I'm used to. I think I would gain imposing some stricter rules at my tables concerning Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found the best way is to impose a rule by asking my players for help. Rather than say &quot;no retainers&quot; or whatever, say &quot;Look guys, when three of you all bring in 1-2 more guys to join every combat, it bogs everything down hard and I simply can't run it. I promise you that you're not wasting points buying them, but unless they're effectively replacing you in the combat, they can't join in every fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're usually pretty understanding about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T22:48:55-07:00","id":1392761,"title":"","content":"Combat is pretty straight forward and pretty much any solar worth their salt can hold their own <br /> at chargen you can have 20 soak 9 parry without even using excellencies as your enemies flounder to hit you pouring motes of essence into their own excellencies as they are rolling at a -6 dice pool penalty to even swing provided they can even stand up at all rolling at a -9 dice penalty at you as you pile on the initiative gain as you whittle their willpower down and laugh as they cant even touch you and fall flat even if they do manage to touch you, you wear them down as you gain positive mote regen economy and hit them for double damage on decisives straight out of character gen doesnt matter if you are outnumbered or what battle groups and they turn on each other fighting themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T00:41:16-07:00","id":1392771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392703#post1392703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've found the best way is to impose a rule by asking my players for help. Rather than say &quot;no retainers&quot; or whatever, say &quot;Look guys, when three of you all bring in 1-2 more guys to join every combat, it bogs everything down hard and I simply can't run it. I promise you that you're not wasting points buying them, but unless they're effectively replacing you in the combat, they can't join in every fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're usually pretty understanding about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't even think of asking them actually I'm more used to be the &quot;whatever happens roll with it&quot; ST but I find it harder and harder to go by that rule when it concerns certain systemic aspect of the game. <br /> <br /> I certainly would gain by trying to fix some rules with the players. I do it but usually for more narrative points (&quot;tell me if you want to leave the jungles so I can prepare some scenarios&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T05:32:27-07:00","id":1392788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392703#post1392703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've found the best way is to impose a rule by asking my players for help. Rather than say &quot;no retainers&quot; or whatever, say &quot;Look guys, when three of you all bring in 1-2 more guys to join every combat, it bogs everything down hard and I simply can't run it. I promise you that you're not wasting points buying them, but unless they're effectively replacing you in the combat, they can't join in every fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're usually pretty understanding about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, especially when each non combat monster that you cant defend other literally gives the opposing team free initiative that they will in turn throw a pebble or bare fist at you with a decisive attack out right one shotting you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T05:53:09-07:00","id":1392789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392761#post1392761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat is pretty straight forward and pretty much any solar worth their salt can hold their own<br /> at chargen you can have 20 soak 9 parry without even using excellencies as your enemies flounder to hit you pouring motes of essence into their own excellencies as they are rolling at a -6 dice pool penalty to even swing provided they can even stand up at all rolling at a -9 dice penalty at you as you pile on the initiative gain as you whittle their willpower down and laugh as they cant even touch you and fall flat even if they do manage to touch you, you wear them down as you gain positive mote regen economy and hit them for double damage on decisives straight out of character gen doesnt matter if you are outnumbered or what battle groups and they turn on each other fighting themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>no one is suggesting a Solar <i>can't</i> hold their own, the problem is &quot;Solars&quot; can go in about a dozen directions and a lot of those directions aren't combat, which makes balancing things really difficult. In a party of Kratos McSephiroth, Hannibal Bonaparte, and Sherlock Hamilton, 2 out of 3 are going to completely crush combat and one of them is going to try not to die until its over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:59:59-07:00","id":1392846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392430#post1392430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to disagree quite a bit with you about one specific thing : I think combat is long in Exalted, even when it's supposed to be simple, and that makes a long 3 combat session with 2 of them are narratively not &quot;interesting&quot; (except if the player had some prior emotional stakes with the guarding cataphracts or the Lorelei).</div> </div> </div> </div>As one of the major advocates for that style of Storytelling, the example of Fair Folk probably isn't the best right now because they've been so heavily characterised as a horde of interchangeable enemies with delusions of grandeur. I'd personally use attacking a Deathlord, Shahan-ya or Great House Matriarch at the seat of their power as my go-to example for a fight that should be broken into stages because they've got access to resources that would be either overwhelming or utterly disappointing to try and run in one combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:47:09-07:00","id":1392864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392846#post1392846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one of the major advocates for that style of Storytelling, the example of Fair Folk probably isn't the best right now because they've been so heavily characterised as a horde of interchangeable enemies with delusions of grandeur. I'd personally use attacking a Deathlord, Shahan-ya or Great House Matriarch at the seat of their power as my go-to example for a fight that should be broken into stages because they've got access to resources that would be either overwhelming or utterly disappointing to try and run in one combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that with the current ressources about the Fair Folk it's hard to discuss on forums with an established complete lore I believe, and Lunars and Deathlords would better fit this role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:31:10-07:00","id":1392880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392846#post1392846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">resources that would be either overwhelming or utterly disappointing to try and run in one combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of where I'm coming from here. It's hard to put into a single picture, but something like <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/42e95c01-0b2a-46b1-bb72-fa6e009d92cb/d1xa7w9-cbfd1268-97b3-4416-9fa0-83813238fdaf.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..-CYF3egy_JSD60QsIGaUwvU8zPpip5btk3L2MGBKSsQ\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, or like <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/warhammerfb/images/0/0b/Tumblr_mzgdpkq7Ni1rn2yg0o1_1280.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20150922080011\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, maybe <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/warhammerfb/images/7/72/Orcs-VS-Dwarfs-1440x2560.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20150718232846\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. I really want to give the sense that the enemy they just defeated was large and powerful enough to legitimately wipe out an empire, and at the same time is diverse and multi-facited.<br /> <br /> It also feels a bit anticlimactic for it to be over in one scene, but maybe that's because my group gets through scenes a lot quicker. Like if we went to fight the Mask of Winters and we just get to his throne room uncontested and fight him and then we win and it's all over I wouldn't feel like we matched our power against the might of Thorns. Not when he has legions of living and undead minions, abyssal sorcerers, behemoths, deathknights, nemisarries, spies, dark artifacts, assassins, necromantic constructs, sorceries, and even more strange things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:22:52-07:00","id":1392898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392789#post1392789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no one is suggesting a Solar <i>can't</i> hold their own, the problem is &quot;Solars&quot; can go in about a dozen directions and a lot of those directions aren't combat, which makes balancing things really difficult. In a party of Kratos McSephiroth, Hannibal Bonaparte, and Sherlock Hamilton, 2 out of 3 are going to completely crush combat and one of them is going to try not to die until its over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly Sherlock Hamilton is an interesting example of a case where the &quot;just have the noncombat characters sit out the fight&quot; solution may be a bad idea, because Hamilton (and Sherlock in some modern versions, I guess) is the type of character to want to get in a fight, but is clearly not a specialist in fighting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As one of the major advocates for that style of Storytelling, the example of Fair Folk probably isn't the best right now because they've been so heavily characterised as a horde of interchangeable enemies with delusions of grandeur. </div> </div> </div>Where is this characterization? Delusions of grandeur, sure, but &quot;interchangeable&quot; wasn't my impression at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:27:10-07:00","id":1392917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392789#post1392789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no one is suggesting a Solar <i>can't</i> hold their own, the problem is &quot;Solars&quot; can go in about a dozen directions and a lot of those directions aren't combat, which makes balancing things really difficult. In a party of Kratos McSephiroth, Hannibal Bonaparte, and Sherlock Hamilton, 2 out of 3 are going to completely crush combat and one of them is going to try not to die until its over.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more than just an issue in combat as well. If a super powerful social enemy makes a big speech, the Zenith Integrity supernal is going to roll their eyes, and then look over to the Integrity 0, Socialize 0 Dawn who's eating the whole thing up. Or the falling rock pillars are going to get deftly dodged by the no-armor night caste thief, while everyone with zero dodge and heavy armor is going to eat those to the face every time.<br /> <br /> Things like War Lion Stance or even just Defend Other in general help a bit in combat at least. It's kind of the Dawn's responsibility to keep the rest of the circle safe from that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T16:48:49-07:00","id":1392936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392898#post1392898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this characterization? Delusions of grandeur, sure, but &quot;interchangeable&quot; wasn't my impression at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>NPC wise there's historically been a lot of variation among Fair Folk courts that doesn't really amount to much from the perspective of outsiders.<br /> There's at least 4 of the Fair Folk signature characters in <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/42e95c01-0b2a-46b1-bb72-fa6e009d92cb/d1xa7w9-cbfd1268-97b3-4416-9fa0-83813238fdaf.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..-CYF3egy_JSD60QsIGaUwvU8zPpip5btk3L2MGBKSsQ\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> image, most people would struggle to tell you how they were meaningfully different from each other. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-30-2020, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:53:56-07:00","id":1392957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392789#post1392789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no one is suggesting a Solar <i>can't</i> hold their own, the problem is &quot;Solars&quot; can go in about a dozen directions and a lot of those directions aren't combat, which makes balancing things really difficult. In a party of Kratos McSephiroth, Hannibal Bonaparte, and Sherlock Hamilton, 2 out of 3 are going to completely crush combat and one of them is going to try not to die until its over.</div> </div> </div> </div>you spelted being the target of the war lion stance wrong<br /> <br /> Also every character should have a combat shtick even if its just 2 or 3 charms you can have 3 charms in thrown and do double damage with full excellency and impose a -3 crippling penalty while being defended by your combat monster dawn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T18:06:55-07:00","id":1392961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392957#post1392957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also every character should have a combat shtick even if its just 2 or 3 charms you can have 3 charms in thrown and do double damage with full excellency and impose a -3 crippling penalty while being defended by your combat monster dawn</div> </div> </div> </div>What 3 thrown charms let you double damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T21:38:57-07:00","id":1392997,"title":"","content":"two deep cascade of cutting terror and its 4 deep for joint wound attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:17:27-07:00","id":1393005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1392997#post1392997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two deep cascade of cutting terror and its 4 deep for joint wound attack</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If successful, the attack is joined by dozens or hundreds of copied weapons, striking points all around the target, doing twice the damage successes to all <b>significant objects and insignificant opponents</b> within short range of the initial strike.&quot;<br /> <br /> That charm does double damage to like, the table, and the weaponless bartender who didn't actually roll join battle, it does no extra damage to either your primary target or anyone surrounding them who's actually rolled into the initiative. It's a once per fight full excellency that costs 5m 1wp instead of 10m, and is undodgable. It's very good, but it's not <i>that </i>good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:34:25-07:00","id":1393026,"title":"","content":"Launching from medium or long range, without needing to aim-action, on the first strike, is rather nice too. If you win the join battle roll.<br /> <br /> If there is a piece of scenery you need to demolish, or a crowd you need to disperse, it can make for a very impressive entrance, rescue, or terror attack.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, it is not a damage multiplier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 05-31-2020, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:09:55-07:00","id":1393052,"title":"","content":"I tend to advise Solar non-combatants to at least pick up Reed in the Wind, I kinda wish other splats had a version of it since it's a good way to acquaint a new or returning player with initiative as a combat resource and having it tends to ensure that the character in question will have a decent dice pool for disengage actions as well as being a prerequisite for most of Solar Dodge if they want to investigate that further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:19:30-07:00","id":1393084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1393026#post1393026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Launching from medium or long range, without needing to aim-action, on the first strike, is rather nice too. If you win the join battle roll.<br /> <br /> If there is a piece of scenery you need to demolish, or a crowd you need to disperse, it can make for a very impressive entrance, rescue, or terror attack.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, it is not a damage multiplier.</div> </div> </div> </div>sounds like it should be a thing, theres one for melee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:28:46-07:00","id":1393134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1393084#post1393084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sounds like it should be a thing, theres one for melee</div> </div> </div> </div>Falling Icicle Strike?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:41:51-07:00","id":1393138,"title":"","content":"the Exalt must succeed at an ambush","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T12:14:02-07:00","id":1393169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cypheriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391070-question-about-3-edition-combat-system?p=1393138#post1393138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Exalt must succeed at an ambush</div> </div> </div> </div>The melee one uses your movement action, and must target an enemy at Short range, no closer or further. Needing to succeed at an ambush is just the restrictions put on the thrown one. You can get an ambush mid-combat with Crimson Razor Wind, but that also costs 14m 1wp, before considering any excellencies, so probably closer to 34m 1wp or something since it's two attacks. It's extremely powerful, but you only get to do it once in a combat.<br /> <br /> Which, again, is why you need more than one scene. A player with ten thrown charms can just spend 34m 1wp and end pretty much end anything. If you want a sense of danger the PCs need to not have the freedom to spend their whole motepool and willpower stock in every combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}